                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nThe intensely bright object formed when a star explodes is not a red giant or a white dwarf, as these are stages in the life cycle of a star and do not result from an explosion. \n\nA nova is a sudden brightening of a star due to a thermonuclear explosion on its surface, but it is not as powerful as a supernova. \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is C) supernova, as it is the most powerful and luminous explosion in the universe, resulting from the catastrophic collapse of a massive star or the merger of two stars.",
