                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nStep 1: What are fossils?\nFossils are the remains or traces of ancient organisms that have been preserved in rocks or other geological materials.\n\nStep 2: What are dinosaurs?\nDinosaurs were a group of reptiles that lived millions of years ago and are now extinct.\n\nStep 3: Where can we find fossils of dinosaurs?\nFossils of dinosaurs are typically found in rocks in the ground. This is because when a dinosaur dies, its body may be buried by sediment, such as sand or mud. Over time, the sediment hardens into rock, preserving the bones or other remains of the dinosaur.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is D) rocks in the ground.",
                        "answers": [
