                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": " \n\nFirst, we need to identify what a fossil is. A fossil is the preserved remains of an organism. This can include the organism's bones, teeth, skin, and other tissues. \n\nNow that we know what a fossil is, we can think about where they might be found. Fossils can be found in the water of oceans, the ice on ponds, the trunks of trees, and rocks in the ground. \n\nThe most likely place to find fossils of dinosaurs is in rocks in the ground. This is because over time, the soft tissues of an organism will decompose, leaving behind the harder parts, like bones and teeth. Rocks can help to preserve these remains.",
                        "answers": [
