                        "cot": "\n\n1. A layer of sediment is deposited on the ocean floor.\n2. The next step in the formation of sedimentary rocks is typically burial, as more layers of sediment accumulate on top of the initial layer.\n3. Over time, the weight of the overlying sediment compacts the lower layers, squeezing out any water and air pockets and causing the sediment to become more tightly packed.\n4. This process, known as lithification, can also involve the cementation of the sediment particles by minerals such as calcite or silica.\n5. Heating may play a role in the formation of some sedimentary rocks, such as those formed from organic matter (e.g. coal), but it is not typically the next step after sediment deposition.\n6. Erosion and weathering are processes that occur prior to sediment deposition, as they involve the breakdown and transport of rock and sediment materials.",
