                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nStep 1: Identify the process that occurs when a forest habitat is destroyed.\n\nWhen a forest habitat is destroyed, the trees and other vegetation are typically removed or burned. This process releases carbon dioxide (CO2) into the atmosphere.\n\nStep 2: Determine which gas is increased in the atmosphere as a result of the destruction of a forest habitat.\n\nBased on Step 1, we can conclude that the destruction of a forest habitat will increase the amount of CO2 in the atmosphere. Therefore, the correct answer is A) CO2.",
