                        "cot": "\n\n1. The troposphere is the lowest layer of the Earth's atmosphere, where weather occurs and temperature decreases with altitude. \n2. The stratosphere is the layer above the troposphere, where the ozone layer is located and temperature increases with altitude. \n3. The mesosphere is the layer above the stratosphere, where temperature decreases with altitude. \n4. The thermosphere is the layer above the mesosphere, where temperature increases with altitude due to the absorption of solar radiation. \n\nBased on this information, we can eliminate options A, B, and C as they do not fit the description of the summit of Mount Everest having a decreasing temperature with altitude. Therefore, the correct answer is D) troposphere.",
