                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "it is important to note that the end-Permian extinction is still a topic of debate among scientists and there is no one definitive answer. However, one hypothesis is that extensive glaciation could have disrupted ocean ecosystems by producing a steep drop in ocean salinity and density. This is because as glaciers form on land, they remove freshwater from the ocean, causing the remaining seawater to become more saline and denser. This can affect the circulation of ocean currents and the mixing of nutrients, which can have negative impacts on marine life. Additionally, the formation and melting of glaciers can cause rapid changes in sea level, which can also have significant impacts on marine ecosystems.",
