                    {
                        "id": "a853beec-dbc4-47b8-913d-5cf3dbcc67a5",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": null,
                        "cot_trigger": "zhou-01",
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nStep 1: Define ocean currents\nOcean currents are the continuous, directed movement of ocean water that flows in a particular direction.\n\nStep 2: Define the Gulf Stream\nThe Gulf Stream is a warm ocean current that flows from the Gulf of Mexico through the Atlantic Ocean towards Europe.\n\nStep 3: How do ocean currents affect world climate?\nOcean currents affect world climate by transferring heat to and from various regions. The Gulf Stream, for example, carries warm water from the Gulf of Mexico to the North Atlantic, which helps to moderate the climate of Western Europe. Without the Gulf Stream, the climate of Western Europe would be much colder.\n\nStep 4: Eliminate incorrect options\nOption A is incorrect because ocean currents do not spread plant and animal life over a wider area. Option B is incorrect because ocean currents do not ensure ocean density is not the same globally. Option C is incorrect because ocean currents do not carry sediment from rivers and inland basins.\n\nStep 5: Select the correct answer\nThe correct answer is D) transferring heat to and from various regions.",
