                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "it is important to note that all of the options listed are true to some extent. However, the most direct and significant impact of ocean currents on world climate is option D: transferring heat to and from various regions. Ocean currents can transport warm water from the tropics to higher latitudes, which can help to moderate temperatures in those regions. For example, the Gulf Stream brings warm water from the Gulf of Mexico up along the east coast of North America, which helps to keep places like the UK and Scandinavia much warmer than they would be otherwise. Similarly, cold water currents can bring cooler temperatures to regions that would otherwise be much warmer. Overall, ocean currents play a crucial role in regulating global climate patterns.",
