                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nOption A is partially correct, as ocean currents can indeed spread plant and animal life over a wider area. However, this is not the primary way in which ocean currents affect world climate.\n\nOption B is also partially correct, as ocean currents do play a role in maintaining differences in ocean density around the world. However, this is not the primary way in which ocean currents affect world climate either.\n\nOption C is not correct, as ocean currents are not primarily responsible for carrying sediment from rivers and inland basins.\n\nOption D is the correct answer. Ocean currents play a crucial role in transferring heat to and from various regions, which in turn affects global climate patterns. For example, the Gulf Stream carries warm water from the tropics to the North Atlantic, which helps to moderate temperatures in Europe. Similarly, the Antarctic Circumpolar Current helps to distribute cold water around the globe, which affects ocean temperatures and weather patterns.",
