                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nFirst, we know that cold air is denser than warm air. This means that cold air will tend to sink and flow downhill, while warm air rises and flows uphill. \n\nSecond, we know that air pressure decreases with altitude. This means that the air pressure at the top of a mountain will be lower than the air pressure in a valley below. \n\nPutting these two facts together, we can conclude that when cold air is at the tops of mountains, it will flow toward areas of lower pressure in valleys. Therefore, the correct answer is A) will flow toward areas of lower pressure in valleys. \n\nOption B is incorrect because cold air will not flow toward areas of higher pressure. Option C is partially correct, but it is not the main reason why cold air flows downhill. Option D is completely unrelated to the question and can be eliminated.",
