                        "cot": "\n\nStep 1: Define the terms.\n\n- Freezing: the process of water turning into ice due to a decrease in temperature.\n- Expanding: the process of something increasing in size or volume.\n- Water: a colorless, transparent, odorless liquid that forms the seas, lakes, rivers, and rain and is the basis of the fluids of living organisms.\n- Cracks: a narrow opening or fissure in a rock or other hard material.\n\nStep 2: Analyze the process.\n\nWater can seep into the cracks of rocks. When the temperature drops, the water freezes and expands, causing the cracks to widen. This process repeats over time, causing the rock to break apart.\n\nStep 3: Identify the geological process.\n\nThe process described above is an example of weathering, which is the breakdown of rocks, soils, and minerals through physical, chemical, and biological processes. In this case, the physical process of freezing and expanding water is causing the rock to break apart.\n\nTherefore, the answer is A) weathering.",
