                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nA) A high pressure area develops. - This is not a correct explanation as high pressure areas do not necessarily cause a decrease in hurricane force.\n\nB) The sea level rises on the coast. - This is also not a correct explanation as rising sea levels would not cause a decrease in hurricane force.\n\nC) The winds start to spin clockwise. - This is not a correct explanation as hurricanes always spin counterclockwise in the Northern Hemisphere and clockwise in the Southern Hemisphere.\n\nD) The supply of warm, moist air decreases. - This is the correct explanation. Hurricanes are fueled by warm, moist air over the ocean. As they move over land, they lose their source of warm, moist air and gradually weaken. Therefore, option D is the correct answer.",
