                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nThe correct answer is C) heat energy.\n\nHere's why:\n\n- When a lightbulb is lit, it uses electrical energy to heat up a filament inside the bulb.\n- As the filament heats up, it begins to glow and emit light energy.\n- However, not all of the electrical energy is converted into light energy. Some of it is lost as heat energy, which is why lightbulbs can get hot to the touch.\n- Chemical energy is the energy stored in the bonds between atoms and molecules, and is not involved in the process of lighting a lightbulb.\n- Magnetic energy is the energy associated with magnetic fields, and is not involved in the process of lighting a lightbulb.\n- Mechanical energy is the energy associated with motion and movement, and is not involved in the process of lighting a lightbulb.",
