                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nThe correct answer is A) tidal energy and hydropower.\n\nHere's why:\n\n- Gravitational energy is the potential energy stored in an object due to its position in a gravitational field. When this object moves, the potential energy is converted into kinetic energy, which can be harnessed to generate electricity.\n- Tidal energy is a form of hydropower that uses the gravitational pull of the moon and the sun to create tides in the ocean. These tides can be captured by turbines and converted into electricity.\n- Hydropower is another form of energy that uses the gravitational potential energy of water stored in dams or reservoirs. When the water is released, it flows through turbines and generates electricity.\n- Geothermal energy is generated by the heat of the Earth's core, and it does not rely on gravitational energy to produce electricity.\n- Wind energy is generated by the kinetic energy of wind, which is caused by differences in air pressure and temperature. While wind turbines do use gravity to stay upright, they do not rely on gravitational energy to generate electricity.\n\nTherefore, the only alternative energy resources that use gravitational energy to make electricity are tidal energy and hydropower, making option A the correct answer.",
