                        "cot": "\n\nFirst, we need to understand what potential energy is. Potential energy is the energy that an object has due to its position or configuration. In the case of a roller coaster, potential energy is the energy that the coaster has due to its height above the ground.\n\nNext, we need to consider the roller coaster's motion. As the coaster climbs up the hill, it is gaining height and therefore potential energy. Once it reaches the top of the hill, it has the maximum height and therefore the maximum potential energy.\n\nTherefore, the answer is B) at the top of the highest hill.",
