                        "cot": "\n\nPlants that can live in sandy soils are adapted to the specific conditions of that environment. Sandy soils are well-draining and have low water-holding capacity, which means that they dry out quickly. Therefore, plants that can live in sandy soils must be able to withstand dry conditions. \n\nOption D) dry conditions is the correct answer. \n\nOption A) fires is not necessarily related to sandy soils. \n\nOption B) salt tolerance is more related to plants that grow in saline soils or coastal areas. \n\nOption C) cold temperatures are not necessarily related to sandy soils either.",
