                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nStep 1: Identify the key characteristic of sandy soils\nSandy soils are characterized by their large particle size and low water-holding capacity. This means that they drain quickly and do not retain moisture well.\n\nStep 2: Consider what types of environmental conditions plants in sandy soils would need to withstand\nPlants in sandy soils would need to be able to survive in dry conditions, as the soil does not hold onto moisture well. They may also need to be able to tolerate high levels of sunlight and heat, as sandy soils can become quite hot. Additionally, sandy soils may contain high levels of salt, which can be damaging to some plants.\n\nStep 3: Evaluate the answer choices\nA) Fires: While some plants may be adapted to survive fires, this is not a characteristic that is specifically related to sandy soils.\nB) Salt: This is a possibility, as sandy soils may contain high levels of salt.\nC) Cold temperatures: This is not a characteristic that is specifically related to sandy soils.\nD) Dry conditions: This is a key characteristic of sandy soils, as discussed in Step 2.\n\nStep 4: Choose the best answer\nBased on our analysis, the best answer is D) dry conditions. Plants that can live in sandy soils are likely adapted to survive in dry conditions, as sandy soils do not retain moisture well. While some plants in sandy soils may also be able to tolerate high levels of salt, this is not a characteristic that is unique to sandy soils.",
