                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nA) Laying eggs to reproduce: This is an innate behavior that is genetically programmed in animals that reproduce through laying eggs. It is not a learned behavior.\n\nB) Having hollow, light-weight bones: This is a physical characteristic that is determined by genetics and is not a behavior, let alone a learned behavior.\n\nC) Avoiding insects that taste bad: This is a learned behavior. Animals may learn through trial and error that certain insects taste bad and are not worth eating, and they may avoid them in the future.\n\nD) Having white feathers on the throat: This is a physical characteristic that is determined by genetics and is not a behavior, let alone a learned behavior.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is C) avoiding insects that taste bad, as it involves a learned behavior.",
