                        "cot": "\n\nThe correct answer is B) endothermic.\n\nHere's why:\n\n- Exothermic reactions release heat, meaning they produce warmer temperatures. This is the opposite of what the question is asking for.\n- Suspension refers to a mixture of two substances, one of which is finely dispersed in the other but not dissolved. This is not related to the temperature of a chemical reaction.\n- Vaporization refers to the process of a liquid turning into a gas. While this can be related to temperature, it is not a type of chemical reaction.\n- Endothermic reactions absorb heat, meaning they produce colder temperatures. This matches the description given in the question.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is B) endothermic.",
