                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nThe answer is A) condensation.\n\nHere's the reasoning:\n\nWhen the heat energy of a gas is decreased, its particles lose kinetic energy and slow down. As a result, the gas molecules move closer together and the intermolecular forces between them become stronger.\n\nIf the temperature of the gas is lowered enough, the intermolecular forces can become strong enough to overcome the kinetic energy of the gas molecules, causing them to stick together and form a liquid. This process is called condensation.\n\nTherefore, decreasing the heat energy of a gas can result in condensation, but not in evaporation (which requires an increase in heat energy), radiation (which is a form of energy transfer, not a change in state), or vaporization (which requires an increase in heat energy).",
                        "answers": [
