                        "cot": " \n\nWe know that electrical wires are coated with a material. This material is either rubber or plastic. \n\nWe also know that this material must be a good insulator. This is because if the material was a good conductor, then the electrical current would flow through the material and not through the wire. \n\nThis means that the material must be a bad conductor, or an insulator. \n\nWe also know that the material must be a good resistors. This is because if the material was a good resistor, then it would resist the flow of electrical current and the wire would not work properly. \n\nThis means that the material must be a bad resistor, or an insulator. \n\nTherefore, the material must be an insulator.",
