                        "cot": "\n\nElectrical wires are used to transmit electricity from one point to another. If the wire was made of a material that conducts electricity easily, such as metal, the electricity would flow out of the wire and into the surrounding environment, causing a short circuit or even a fire. Therefore, electrical wires are coated with a material that does not conduct electricity easily, known as an insulator. \n\nRubber and plastic are both good insulators, which is why they are commonly used to coat electrical wires. This prevents the electricity from escaping the wire and ensures that it reaches its intended destination. \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is C) insulators.",
