                        "cot": "\n\nStep 1: Understand the concept of chemical property\nChemical property refers to the ability of a substance to undergo a chemical change or reaction and form new substances with different properties. \n\nStep 2: Analyze the options\nA) Density: Density is a physical property that describes the amount of mass per unit volume of a substance. It does not involve any chemical change or reaction. Therefore, it is not a chemical property.\nB) Flammability: Flammability is the ability of a substance to burn or ignite when exposed to a flame or heat. This property involves a chemical change or reaction, as the substance reacts with oxygen in the air to produce new substances. Therefore, it is a chemical property.\nC) Color: Color is a physical property that describes the appearance of a substance. It does not involve any chemical change or reaction. Therefore, it is not a chemical property.\nD) Brittleness: Brittleness is the tendency of a substance to break or shatter when subjected to stress or pressure. It does not involve any chemical change or reaction. Therefore, it is not a chemical property.\n\nStep 3: Conclusion\nOut of the given options, only flammability involves a chemical change or reaction and is therefore a chemical property. Therefore, the correct answer is B) flammability.",
